{{also|hög|høg}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|hogg|lang=ang}}, {{term|hocg||hog|lang=ang}}, possibly from {{etyl|non}} {{term|hǫggva||to strike, chop, cut|lang=non|sc=Latinx}}, from {{proto|Germanic|hawwanan|to hew, forge|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|kowə-|to beat, hew, forge|lang=en}}. Cognate with Old High German {{term|houwan|lang=goh}}, Old Saxon {{term|hauwan|lang=osx}}, Old English {{term|heawan|hēawan|lang=ang}} (English {{term|hew}}). "Hog" originally meant a [[castrate]]d male pig. (Compare "[[hoggett]]" for a castrated male sheep.) More at {{l|en|hew}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/hɒɡ/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/hɑɡ/|/hɔːɡ/}}
* {{audio|en-us-hog.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɒɡ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any animal belonging to the [[Suidae]] family of mammals, especially the [[pig]], the [[wart hog]], and the [[boar]].
# A [[greedy]] person; one who refuses to share.
# {{slang}} A large motorcycle, particularly a [[w:Harley Davidson|Harley-Davidson]].

